comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-17T00:41:32.325Z","harness:claude-code","Residuals for the adversarial corpus, from the pm-ycgb5g and pm-3fbj1f review loop (Codex rounds 1 to 3, 2026-11-17). (1) password_assignment follows references nested one level in an unquoted value. A literal default nested three or more levels deep (password=${A:-${B:-${C:-<literal>}}}), or a literal after such a reference, is missed in the flat and quoted-key spellings, while quoted values and elements follow any depth through expandRuntimeReferences. Closing it needs a code tokenizer in place of the declared regex value grammar. (2) An unquoted password value may hold at most four whitespace-free quoted pieces; a literal spread over more pieces is missed. That bound keeps each structured scan to a few later keys. (3) A bare $VAR is still read as literal text by password_assignment and as a reference by credential_key_assignment; pm-hw00c2 owns aligning the two.\n"
  "2026-11-17T01:18:05.330Z","harness:claude-code","Progress from the pm-ycgb5g branch (not closing this item): the second criterion, judging escaped JSON literals on their decoded original, is implemented for every key-named rule. decodeQuotedLiteral returns both the neutralized reading the value grammar reads and the decoded original at the same length. Capture offsets (d flag) map the matched span back, and acceptsSecretMatch then judges the original, so credential_key_assignment measures entropy on the decoded original value. The other criteria remain open: a declared adversarial corpus with a measured escape rate, and env-style all-caps keys.\n"
  "2026-11-17T02:43:46.888Z","harness:claude-code","Residual (4), from the CodeRabbit review of PR 1745: an escaped quoted literal followed directly by an unquoted suffix in the same value (a quoted key whose value is an escaped literal glued to eight more literal characters) has only the escaped literal judged. The suffix is never measured, and the flat rule cannot match a quoted key. Main behaves the same. Closing it needs a mixed literal model: the decoded literal's characters are data and the suffix is text with shell quoting.\n"
body: ""
